{"id":"PPG_V2.0__compounds__PPG_diagnostc","collection":"PPG_V2.0","category":"compounds","source_path":"PPG_V2.0/compounds/PPG_diagnostc.json","root_names":["PPG::PPG_diagnostc"],"counts":{"nodes":4,"connections":30,"values":16,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Diagnostic display for PPG specific face tags.","documentation_search":"PPG Diagnostic Diagnostic display for PPG specific face tags. Inputs Mesh The input geometry. Soften Harden Edges Enable Soften Harden Enable. Angle Angle for Soften/Harden. Color Tags These settings create random colors for all PPG specific face tags. IMPORTANT: To create per-face colors the polygons are detached and assigned different shaders. For the final geometry you should turn colors OFF. Enable Enable colors. Hue Range 360 means the whole color range. Hue Offset Shift a smaller color range. Hue Random Seed Random seed. Saturation Base Base saturation. Sat Random Max random amount added on top of base. Sat Random Seed Random seed. Brightness Brightness of all colors. Default Tag Color The color of the \"Default\" face tag (\"--\"). All random colors will be a color, i.e. not grey. Face Tag Names Display the names of the face tags in 3D on the polygons. Face Tag Selection Select which face tags to display. Tag Expression Filter the tag names to display only specific ones or to exclude some. Default is \" \" to display ALL face tags. A \"!\" at the start of the tag name means to exclude that tag. Face IDs An array of face IDs. Invert Invert the output of the face selection. Tag Names Settings to format the tag display. Offset along Normal Moves the label along the respective face normal. Line Color Text Color. Offset Additional Transformation. Rotation Additional Rotation. Scale Size of the label. Max Labels Max number of labels to display. Set this higher if you need to see more labels. Information What to display. Show Face Tag Show the name of the tag. Show face ID Show the number of that face. Tutorial","port_names":["angle","brightness","default_tag_color","enable","enable_soften_harden","face_indices","face_labels","filter_field","hue_offset","hue_random_seed","hue_range","invert","line_color","max_labels","mesh","offset","offset_along_normal","out_mesh","rotation","sat_random","sat_random_seed","saturation_base","scale","show_face_ID","show_face_tag","tag_expression"],"node_types_search":["Core::Logic::if","Geometry::Mesh::soften_harden_edges","PPG::assign_random_colors","PPG::display_face_tags"],"dependencies_search":["PPG::assign_random_colors","PPG::display_face_tags"],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"PPG::PPG_diagnostc","uri_imported":"file:///PPG_diagnostc.json","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/ENU/PPG_diagnostic.md"},"documentation_file":"PPG_V2.0/docs/ENU/PPG_diagnostic.md","documentation":"# PPG Diagnostic\nDiagnostic display for PPG specific face tags.\n\n## Inputs\n\n### Mesh\nThe input geometry.\n\n## Soften Harden Edges\n\n### Enable Soften Harden\nEnable.\n\n### Angle\nAngle for Soften/Harden.\n\n## Color Tags\nThese settings create random colors for all PPG specific face tags.<br>\nIMPORTANT: To create per-face colors the polygons are detached and assigned different shaders. For the final geometry you should turn colors OFF.\n\n\n### Enable\nEnable colors.\n\n### Hue Range\n360 means the whole color range.\n\n### Hue Offset\nShift a smaller color range.\n\n### Hue Random Seed\nRandom seed.\n\n### Saturation Base\nBase saturation.\n\n### Sat Random\nMax random amount added on top of base.\n\n### Sat Random Seed\nRandom seed.\n\n### Brightness\nBrightness of all colors.\n\n### Default Tag Color\nThe color of the \"Default\" face tag (\"--\").<br>\nAll random colors will be a color, i.e. not grey.\n\n## Face Tag Names\nDisplay the names of the face tags in 3D on the polygons.\n\n## Face Tag Selection\nSelect which face tags to display.\n\n### Tag Expression\nFilter the tag names to display only specific ones or to exclude some.<br>\nDefault is \"*\" to display ALL face tags.<br>\nA \"!\" at the start of the tag name means to exclude that tag.\n\n### Face IDs\nAn array of face IDs.\n\n### Invert\nInvert the output of the face selection.\n\n## Tag Names\nSettings to format the tag display.\n\n### Offset along Normal\nMoves the label along the respective face normal.\n\n### Line Color\nText Color.\n\n### Offset\nAdditional Transformation.\n\n### Rotation\nAdditional Rotation.\n\n### Scale\nSize of the label.\n\n### Max Labels\nMax number of labels to display.<br>\nSet this higher if you need to see more labels.\n\n## Information\nWhat to display.\n\n### Show Face Tag\nShow the name of the tag.\n\n### Show face ID\nShow the number of that face.\n\n\n\n## Tutorial\n\n<br><br>","ports":[{"name":"out_mesh","direction":"output","type":null},{"name":"mesh","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"enable_soften_harden","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"true"},{"name":"angle","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"30f"},{"name":"enable","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"true"},{"name":"hue_range","direction":"input","type":null,"default":"360f"},{"name":"hue_offset","direction":"input","type":null,"default":"0f"},{"name":"hue_random_seed","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"5"},{"name":"saturation_base","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.5f"},{"name":"sat_random","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.5f"},{"name":"sat_random_seed","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"0"},{"name":"brightness","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.319999993f"},{"name":"default_tag_color","direction":"input","type":null,"default":{"x":"0.159999996f","y":"0.159999996f","z":"0.159999996f"}},{"name":"tag_expression","direction":"input","type":"string","default":"* !inst_* !--"},{"name":"face_indices","direction":"input","type":null},{"name":"invert","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"false"},{"name":"offset_along_normal","direction":"inp